	"note": "云台 (native:lancheng/deck, whirl, cloud_edge; 第十章 C): a white stone shelf hung over the cloud sea on top of the 风铃阁, no rail, worn smooth by the wind, moss in the joints on the lee; the whirlwind in its north middle with 旋芒 turning point down in it, lit white by itself (a layout stage prop: gone once the sword has its hand, the worn ring left); the cloud lapping at every lip, far mountains slipping back below (the town moving on the wind); stone lanterns, pale 风灯 at night; strings of small bells from the pavilion's top eave over the stair's head. Warm white and verdigris and faded red cord, never a flat grey.",
